    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the existing snapshot-at-creation pattern used by `AssignNamesakeCount` so the flag is persisted and reads back correctly via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` boolean `bulkSignupWarning` to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions).\n- **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column. Tests run on hsqldb; the others are updated for consistency. Existing `data.sql` inserts use explicit column lists, so the new nullable column is safe.\n- **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function that counts existing owners on this owner's effective business day (the exact counting `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` uses) and sets the flag `true` when that count is `> 80`. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count reflects only pre-existing owners.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignBulkSignupWarning` step between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors (it needs the registration date already set by `applyRegistrationDate`).\n\nThe `bulkSignupWarning` value is a snapshot frozen at creation \u2014 counted the same way as the per-day cap \u2014 so a fresh create under the threshold returns `false` (verified by the acceptance test) and the `>80` branch shares that same accumulation path.",
